import numpy as np
DESCRIPTION = (
 "Input = function f on positions 0..5 (tokens 0..5). Two unmasked attention layers, one head each, residual width 8, "
 "readout at the last position only. LAYER 0 (query p, key j): the score is the bilinear form E[p]@A0@E[j] with "
 "E[p]=WE[x_p]+WP[p]. Because E splits into a token part and a position part, the score splits EXACTLY into four 6x6 "
 "tables: G[token_p,token_j] + Bt[token_p,j] + Ct[p,token_j] + Dt[p,j]; all four are needed and Dt (positions) is the "
 "largest. Weights a0[p,:]=softmax_j(score). The added value at p is the a0-weighted average of V0(j)=TE[x_j]+TP[j] "
 "(a token table plus a position table), o0[p]=sum_j a0[p,j]V0(j); residual r0=WE[x_p]+WP[p]+o0. LAYER 1 (no mask, so "
 "every position queries, but only position 5 reaches the readout): score s1[p,j]=r0[p]@A1 . r0[j], a1=softmax_j, "
 "o1[p]=(sum_j a1[p,j] r0[j])@P1, r1=r0+o1. READOUT logits=r1[5]@WU, decision=argmax. Nothing is thresholded or "
 "case-analysed: every logit is a smooth linear readout of two attention-weighted averages of token/position tables, so "
 "apparent 'classification' structure (fixed points, cycles, preimage counts) is only emergent. Rules: softmax over "
 "keys, value = weighted average, output = linear map of the last residual.")
